          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "Is JVTO featured in any independent travel guides?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "Yes. Stefan Loose Reiseführer Indonesien: mit Reiseatlas — a German-language Indonesia travel guide — features Ijen Bondowoso Homestay (the founder's 2015 guesthouse, JVTO's historical anchor) on page 287 (ISBN-13 9783770167654). This is non-paid editorial coverage. Publication year and edition are not asserted."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "Has the founder been profiled by national press?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "Yes. Detik.com (one of Indonesia's largest news outlets) profiled Bripka Agung Sambuko in March 2021 in an article about Bondowoso Tourist Police. Radar Jember / Jawa Pos has also covered the formation of the POLPAR unit supporting Ijen Geopark, providing local-press context for the police-led safety model."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "What is the Booking.com 2015 award and how is it evidence?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "Booking.com issued a 2015 Guest Review Award (score 9.4/10) to the guesthouse operated at Jl. Khairil Anwar 102A, Bondowoso — JVTO's pre-incorporation address. The original plaque and shipping label are retained; the shipping label's delivery address matches today's PT office address, establishing unbroken address continuity from 2015 to the current registration."
            }
